    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling Saturday, led by the day's two standout plays: **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Andy Pages** (73.47). **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits immensely from a soft matchup against Chandler, with his score boosted by a favorable 4.92 xERA and a strong 14% platoon edge as he hits second. Similarly, **Andy Pages** exploits a prime matchup against a struggling Sears (5.11 xERA), with the added benefit of wind blowing out, making him a premier start despite the southpaw opposition. While **Gunnar Henderson** faces a trickier test against Lodolo, his elite base production and prime leadoff spot keep his floor high at a 69.41, ensuring he remains a focal point of our offensive engine.\n\nOur bench strategy today emphasizes discipline regarding our 40.0 efficiency floor, most notably regarding the decision to sit **Denzer Guzman**. At 44.48, **Denzer Guzman** was the clear standout among reserves, but he ultimately yielded to the higher projected efficiency of our middle-infield starters. We also remain cautious with **Josh Lowe**, whose base projection is strong, but a move to the nine-hole combined with a tough platoon disadvantage against Suarez drags him down to a 37.17, well below our threshold for active play. \n\nRisk management remains critical as we navigate a few potential pitfalls. **Dominic Smith** is a marginal start at 43.55; his efficiency is depressed by a difficult matchup against the 3.47 xERA of McLean, and he is only active due to the necessity of depth. We are also monitoring **Drake Baldwin**, whose 51.04 score is tempered by the same tough pitching environment. Finally, please note that **Jordan Westburg** remains on the IL, requiring us to extract maximum value from our active roster as we continue to hunt for scarce stolen bases and batting average stability across the rest of the lineup.",
